Z||000001||My7Fieros||06-09-2000||02:01 PM||||No doubt about it, Vettes, especially the new ones, are super cool. In fact Im painting my 88 Formula 2000 Corvette red.<BR>They're overpriced in my opinion though, and Ive never been a fan of the interior of those cars, feels kinda "cheap" for such a nice car. Oh well, prob. wouldnt complain if I had one though! ;-)||||reg||7
Z||000002||fiero56||06-09-2000||04:29 PM||||C5s have been around since '97(3 years for the mathematically challenged <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">). There are a TON of them on the roads. Must see several dozen a day. They do look good though, and I think they are a bargain deal for everything they come with(no, I don't own one). I've only driven a C5 once, but it was one of the strongest pulling cars I have driven. Colors of choice would be black, yellow, or red, in that order.||||reg||1
Z||000003||87ECO5||06-09-2000||08:41 PM||||When you consider the cars it competes against, it's a downright bargain!  I do agree that the interior needs some attention.  Maybe when the C6 debuts after the 2003 50th anniversary.<P>My color choices would be:<P>1.  White with light oak interior<BR>2.  Yellow with graphite interior<BR>3.  Pewter metallic with light oak interior<BR>4.  Navy blue with light oak interior<BR>5.  Forest green with light oak interior||||reg||14
